# MCP server

`mcp/server.py` exposes this agent to Model Context Protocol clients (Claude Desktop, IDEs and
other agents).

| MCP tool | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
{%- for tool in read_tools %}
| `{{ tool.name }}` | {{ tool.description|md }} (read-only) |
{%- endfor %}
{%- if retrieval.enabled %}
| `search_knowledge` | Cited passages from approved sources |
{%- endif %}
| `run_agent` | Run the full agent workflow on a request |
| `get_run` | Read a run's state |

Draft and execute tools are **not** exposed. Side effects only happen through the graph, and
approvals require an approver key on the HTTP API (`POST /v1/runs/{run_id}/approval`). Configure a
shared `CHECKPOINT_BACKEND` (sqlite or postgres) so runs started over MCP can be approved over HTTP.

## Run

```bash
pip install -e ".[mcp]"
python mcp/server.py                                     # stdio
python mcp/server.py --transport streamable-http --port 8001
docker compose --profile mcp up                          # containerised, port 8001
```

## Client configuration

`mcp/mcp.json` is a ready-to-adapt client entry. Run the client from the repository root (or set
`cwd`) so `mcp/server.py` and `data/` resolve.
